false\n   allowed_targets:\n     - \"AGENTS.md, the root document: created when the repository has none, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block, and left alone when it already matches\"\n-    - \"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and removed by default; kept, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given\"\n+    - \"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and replaced by a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer by default. Kept as it is, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given. Created as that pointer when it is absent and the run writes another file.\"\n     - \".codex/AGENTS.md, folded into the block and removed\"\n     - \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md, the generated mirror of a non-empty block; removed when the block is empty\"\n     - \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md, rewritten by its own generator, sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, which this engine calls and never composes a byte of\"\n@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ inputs:\n   dry_run: \"--dry-run prints the plan and its digest, then STATUS=OK without asking a question (default false). The plan call writes nothing either way; the flag only removes the question and the write.\"\n   plan_digest: \"The plan digest the plan printed. It is what makes the approved bytes checkable: the apply recomposes and refuses any digest that no longer matches.\"\n   digest_confirmation: \"true once the operator has answered yes to the plan whose digest was on screen. A plan approved at one tree is never applied at another, because the digest would not match.\"\n-  keep_claude_md: \"--keep-claude-md folds a divergent CLAUDE.md into the block and keeps the file; --remove-claude-md folds it and removes it, which is the default (default false, so removal).\"\n+  keep_claude_md: \"--keep-claude-md folds a divergent CLAUDE.md into the block and keeps the file. --remove-claude-md folds it and leaves a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer, which is the default (default false, so the pointer).\"\n   crea